<p class="section-label">LEADERSHIP + ENGINEERING</p>

<h2>Strategy and implementation should inform each other.</h2>

</div>


<div class="about-copy">

<p class="about-lead">
    I do not view technical leadership and hands-on engineering
    as separate disciplines.
</p>

<p>
    Understanding the architecture makes technology decisions
    stronger. Understanding operations makes architecture more
    realistic. Understanding security makes infrastructure more
    resilient. And understanding the people operating those systems
    makes automation more useful.
</p>

<p>
    That is why I continue to work directly with logs, packet
    captures, authentication flows, infrastructure, cloud services,
    code and diagnostic tools while also working at the
    organizational and strategic level.
</p>

<p>
    The goal is not to be the person performing every technical
    task. The goal is to understand technology deeply enough to
    ask better questions, make better decisions, help engineers
    solve difficult problems and build systems that improve how
    the organization operates.
</p>

</div>

</div>

